From f6397f32467ffe4d27b83595dba96dfdd0424eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taimoor Ul Islam <tislam@iastate.edu>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 13:41:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/52] kaiair: GRK (Gain-Ratio-K) interference model +
 K-adaptation core (Phase 3)

Slow-loop interference-coordination substrate. Given a gain map (per-interferer
G(C,R), expected tx power, activity) and the tolerable interference budget
E_max[I_R] from pktr_ipc, size the exclusion region and derive K = G(T,R)/G(boundary).

- lib/scheduler/kaiair/pktr_grk.h (header-only, pure math): grk_interferer gain-map
  row abstraction; in_exclusion_region() PRK membership (C in ER <=> G(C,R) >= G_TR/K);
  size_exclusion_region() sorts by gain, admits strongest until residual <= budget,
  derives K from the boundary node; interference_error_db() = E_max - I_current (the
  K-adaptation driver). Interference sums in the linear domain.
- pktr_grk_test.cpp: 9 deterministic unit tests (membership, ER sizing in gain order,
  K == G_TR - G_boundary, monotonicity, residual <= budget, IPC->GRK end-to-end).
  All 5 PktR suites pass.

Covers T3.1-T3.2. Consumes the gain map as an abstraction, decoupled from the
signal-map plumbing (T1.3/T1.4). Not yet wired into the scheduler (T3.4) -- unit-
tested only; meaningful HW validation needs a 2nd interfering cell (M2).
